cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use smol or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "smol: a fast Rust reimplementation of the Stringmol automata chemistry"
abstract: >-
  smol reimplements the spatial Stringmol automata chemistry (Hickinbotham, Stepney et al.)
  in Rust, from a description of the model rather than a translation of the C++ code, for long
  and large evolution experiments. The repository also holds a study of parasitism in Stringmol
  that tests the account in Hickinbotham, Stepney & Hogeweg (2021), with every script and raw
  result behind it (docs/parasitism.md, docs/findings.md, experiments/).
authors:
  - family-names: Mold
    given-names: David
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-3441-3506"
version: 0.1.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24443700
date-released: 2026-11-22
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
